{"slug": "furward", "title": "Furward: A cat traveling across China", "banner": {"src": "/images/cs/jd5rnv6AKPp19xSeU9wL7aPikU.webp", "pos": "50% 50%", "h": 480}, "head": {"t": "box", "w": 818, "h": 78, "flex": "column|12px|0px|flex-start|flex-start|nowrap", "clip": 1, "kids": [{"t": "text", "w": 654, "h": 43, "html": "<h1 style=\"font-family:var(--serif);font-size:36px;line-height:43.2px;color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Furward: A cat traveling across China</h1>", "single": true}, {"t": "box", "w": 818, "h": 23, "flex": "row|12px|0px|center|flex-start|nowrap", "clip": 1, "kids": [{"t": "text", "w": 90, "h": 22, "html": "<p style=\"font-family:var(--sans);font-size:14px;line-height:22.4px;color:rgb(138, 138, 138);font-style:italic;letter-spacing:-0.28px\">Game Designer</p>", "single": true}, {"t": "text", "w": 8, "h": 23, "html": "<p style=\"font-family:var(--sans);font-size:15px;line-height:22.5px;color:rgb(203, 203, 203);letter-spacing:-0.3px\">|</p>", "single": true}, {"t": "text", "w": 105, "h": 22, "html": "<p style=\"font-family:var(--sans);font-size:14px;line-height:22.4px;color:rgb(138, 138, 138);font-style:italic;letter-spacing:-0.28px\">July - August 2024</p>", "single": true}, {"t": "text", "w": 8, "h": 23, "html": "<p style=\"font-family:var(--sans);font-size:15px;line-height:22.5px;color:rgb(203, 203, 203);letter-spacing:-0.3px\">|</p>", "single": true}, {"t": "text", "w": 249, "h": 22, "html": "<p style=\"font-family:var(--sans);font-size:14px;line-height:22.4px;color:rgb(138, 138, 138);font-style:italic;letter-spacing:-0.28px\">Procreate, Figma, Adobe Photoshop, Unity</p>", "single": true}], "fill": 1}]}, "layout": {"side": [179, 222], "main": [433, 900], "head": [451, 818], "headTop": 32, "tocW": 150, "tocPad": "50px", "tocGap": "25px", "tocAlign": "center"}, "toc": [{"text": "← Home", "href": "/"}, {"text": "About", "href": "#01-context"}, {"text": "Ideation", "href": "#02-problem"}, {"text": "Iteration", "href": "#03-style"}, {"text": "Animation", "href": "#04-animation"}, {"text": "Expansion", "href": "#05-expansion"}, {"text": "Reflection", "href": "#06-reflection"}], "content": {"t": "box", "w": 900, "h": 6587, "flex": "column|70px|70px 0px 0px|center|center|nowrap", "kids": [{"reveal": 1, "t": "box", "w": 900, "h": 266, "flex": "row|10px|0px|center|center|nowrap", "kids": [{"t": "box", "w": 900, "h": 266, "flex": "row|24px|0px|center|center|nowrap", "kids": [{"t": "box", "w": 900, "h": 266, "flex": "column|0px|0px|flex-start|center|nowrap", "clip": 1, "kids": [{"reveal": 1, "t": "box", "w": 900, "h": 266, "flex": "row|0px|0px|center|center|nowrap", "clip": 1, "kids": [{"bg": "rgb(210, 105, 53)", "t": "box", "w": 3, "h": 266, "clip": 1, "kids": [], "empty": 1}, {"br": "0px 8px 8px 0px", "bg": "rgba(210, 105, 53, 0.05)", "t": "box", "w": 897, "h": 266, "flex": "row|24px|16px 16px 16px 24px|center|flex-start|nowrap", "clip": 1, "kids": [{"t": "box", "w": 417, "h": 189, "flex": "column|24px|0px|flex-start|center|nowrap", "clip": 1, "kids": [{"t": "box", "w": 417, "h": 123, "flex": "column|10px|0px|center|center|nowrap", "clip": 1, "kids": [{"t": "text", "w": 417, "h": 23, "html": "<p style=\"font-family:var(--sans);font-size:15px;line-height:22.5px;color:rgb(77, 77, 77);letter-spacing:-0.3px\"><strong style=\"font-family:var(--sans);font-size:15px;line-height:22.5px;color:rgb(77, 77, 77);font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-0.3px\">Check it Out!</strong></p>", "fill": 1, "single": true}, {"t": "text", "w": 417, "h": 90, "html": "<p style=\"font-family:var(--sans);font-size:15px;line-height:22.5px;color:rgb(77, 77, 77);letter-spacing:-0.3px\">Furward is a a fancy version of Chrome's <em style=\"font-family:var(--sans);font-size:15px;line-height:22.5px;color:rgb(77, 77, 77);font-style:italic;letter-spacing:-0.3px\">no-wifi dino</em> game with a mission to convey the whimsical charms of China. It was designed by yours truly, and developed by my best friend Isamel :)</p>", "fill": 1, "single": false}], "fill": 1}, {"href": "https://jamcats.itch.io/furward", "target": "_blank", "br": "10px", "t": "box", "w": 141, "h": 43, "flex": "column|10px|10px|center|center|nowrap", "clip": 1, "kids": [{"t": "text", "w": 121, "h": 23, "html": "<p style=\"font-family:var(--sans);font-size:15px;line-height:22.5px;color:rgb(210, 105, 53);letter-spacing:-0.3px\">Furward on itch.io</p>", "fill": 1, "single": true}], "btn": {"bd": "rgb(210, 105, 53)", "fg": "rgb(210, 105, 53)", "hbg": "rgb(211, 107, 56)", "hfg": "#fff"}}]}, {"href": "https://jamcats.itch.io/furward", "target": "_blank", "br": "5px", "t": "box", "w": 417, "h": 234, "kids": [{"br": "5px", "t": "img", "w": 417, "h": 234, "src": "/images/cs/kwyzvFIKR7moesNWSSdfStCgfw.webp", "fit": "cover", "pos": "50% 50%", "abs": [0, 0]}], "frame": 1}], "stack": 1}], "fill": 1}], "fill": 1}], "fill": 1}], "fill": 1}, {"reveal": 1, "t": "box", "w": 900, "h": 473, "flex": "column|0px|0px|center|center|nowrap", "kids": [{"t": "box", "w": 900, "h": 473, "flex": "column|10px|0px|center|center|nowrap", "clip": 1, "kids": [{"id": "01-context", "t": "text", "w": 900, "h": 21, "html": "<h5 style=\"font-family:var(--mono);font-size:14px;line-height:21px;color:rgb(210, 105, 53)\">ABOUT</h5>", "fill": 1, "single": true}, {"t": "text", "w": 900, "h": 38, "html": "<h3 style=\"font-family:var(--serif);font-size:24px;line-height:30px;color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">My summers in China…</h3>", "fill": 1, "single": true}, {"t": "text", "w": 900, "h": 42, "html": "<p style=\"font-family:var(--sans);font-size:15px;line-height:22.5px;color:rgb(77, 77, 77);letter-spacing:-0.3px\">Although Furward is simple, it's a project I hold extremely near to my heart. It’s a combination of the four things I’ve loved since childhood: cats, games, art, and summer trips to China</p>", "fill": 1, "single": false}, {"t": "box", "w": 900, "h": 342, "flex": "row|30px|0px|flex-start|center|nowrap", "clip": 1, "kids": [{"t": "box", "w": 435, "h": 342, "flex": "column|0px|0px|center|center|nowrap", "clip": 1, "kids": [{"t": "text", "w": 435, "h": 22, "html": "<p style=\"font-family:var(--sans);font-size:14px;line-height:22.4px;color:rgb(138, 138, 138);font-style:italic;letter-spacing:-0.28px\">DAY MODE</p>", "fill": 1, "single": true}, {"t": "text", "w": 435, "h": 105, "html": "<p style=\"font-family:var(--sans);font-size:15px;line-height:22.5px;color:rgb(77, 77, 77);letter-spacing:-0.3px\">The “day” game mode is inspired by my mom’s home province, Fujian, China. With vivid colours and whimsical tidbits such as the dragon in the lake, missing cat posters, and playful sprites, I wanted to capture the vibrancy and playfulness I experienced the last time I went to Fujian.&nbsp;</p>", "fill": 1, "single": false}, {"br": "8px", "t": "video", "w": 435, "h": 214, "src": "/media/cs/jqOmmSWOdWcZOevkjpPWf9ZKNn0.mp4", "fit": "cover", "poster": "https://framerusercontent.com/images/TUlnC99H5qIRZooUBfSH65B9Kw.png?width=1582&height=780", "fill": 1}]}, {"t": "box", "w": 435, "h": 342, "flex": "column|0px|0px|center|center|nowrap", "clip": 1, "kids": [{"t": "text", "w": 435, "h": 22, "html": "<p style=\"font-family:var(--sans);font-size:14px;line-height:22.4px;color:rgb(138, 138, 138);font-style:italic;letter-spacing:-0.28px\">NIGHT MODE</p>", "fill": 1, "single": true}, {"t": "text", "w": 435, "h": 105, "html": "<p style=\"font-family:var(--sans);font-size:15px;line-height:22.5px;color:rgb(77, 77, 77);letter-spacing:-0.3px\">The “night” game map is inspired by my dad's home city, Shanghai. Keeping up with the playful nature of the countryside, I added a dragon hiding in the water, playful political posters to vote a cat politician into office, and a grandma who wants to go back to the countryside.&nbsp;</p>", "fill": 1, "single": false}, {"br": "8px", "t": "video", "w": 435, "h": 214, "src": "/media/cs/s4OvJwzYjhCHYa72WaRVIpyxwY.mp4", "fit": "cover", "poster": "https://framerusercontent.com/images/3n0vVIQV3lVj7LlnoeySFiu0Vw.png?width=1582&height=780", "fill": 1}]}], "fill": 1, "stack": 1}], "fill": 1}], "fill": 1}, {"reveal": 1, "t": "box", "w": 900, "h": 1286, "flex": "column|32px|0px|center|center|nowrap", "kids": [{"t": "box", "w": 900, "h": 649, "flex": "column|8px|0px|flex-start|center|nowrap", "clip": 1, "kids": [{"id": "02-problem", "t": "text", "w": 900, "h": 21, "html": "<h5 style=\"font-family:var(--mono);font-size:14px;line-height:21px;color:rgb(210, 105, 53)\">IDEATION</h5>", "fill": 1, "single": true}, {"t": "text", "w": 900, "h": 38, "html": "<h3 style=\"font-family:var(--serif);font-size:24px;line-height:30px;color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Telling a personal story</h3>", "fill": 1, "single": true}, {"t": "box", "w": 900, "h": 248, "flex": "row|10px|0px|flex-start|center|nowrap", "kids": [{"t": "text", "w": 445, "h": 231, "html": "<p style=\"font-family:var(--sans);font-size:15px;line-height:22.5px;color:rgb(77, 77, 77);letter-spacing:-0.3px\">My initial concept development was highly non-linear. It involved collecting photo references and sketching in my notebook until an idea started to take shape. I experimented with several elements, including the amount of \"magicality\", characters, and environments. It was easy to get carried away and lost in the ideation process—if I hadn’t made a conscious effort to stop, I could have kept doodling endlessly. After multiple iterations and personal reflection, one thing became clear—I wanted to highlight the countryside, drawing deep inspiration from my home province, Fujian. My personal most magical memories of China were seeing the Chinese countryside during golden hour - the period right before sunset.</p>", "single": false}, {"br": "5px", "t": "box", "w": 445, "h": 248, "kids": [{"br": "5px", "t": "img", "w": 445, "h": 248, "src": "/images/cs/1nx51qXZ2T2L8iBxaevnHzHMj0.webp", "fit": "cover", "pos": "50% 50%", "abs": [0, 0]}], "frame": 1}], "fill": 1, "stack": 1}, {"t": "box", "w": 900, "h": 318, "flex": "row|20px|0px|center|center|nowrap", "kids": [{"br": "5px", "t": "box", "w": 440, "h": 318, "kids": [{"br": "5px", "t": "img", "w": 440, "h": 318, "src": "/images/cs/wKER90wZQSkg3SMXIR2NjRGk.webp", "fit": "cover", "pos": "50% 50%", "abs": [0, 0]}], "frame": 1}, {"br": "5px", "t": "box", "w": 440, "h": 306, "kids": [{"br": "5px", "t": "img", "w": 440, "h": 306, "src": "/images/cs/nNrjGm2Ys73qRa6pdMe3zDM8Fs.webp", "fit": "cover", "pos": "50% 50%", "abs": [0, 0]}], "frame": 1}], "fill": 1, "stack": 1}], "fill": 1}, {"t": "box", "w": 900, "h": 604, "flex": "column|8px|0px|flex-start|center|nowrap", "clip": 1, "kids": [{"t": "text", "w": 136, "h": 38, "html": "<h3 style=\"font-family:var(--serif);font-size:24px;line-height:30px;color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Environment</h3>", "single": true}, {"t": "box", "w": 900, "h": 251, "flex": "row|10px|0px|flex-start|center|nowrap", "kids": [{"t": "text", "w": 445, "h": 189, "html": "<p style=\"font-family:var(--sans);font-size:15px;line-height:22.5px;color:rgb(77, 77, 77);letter-spacing:-0.3px\">I decided to digitally illustrate my first environment sketch as a direct graphic representation of the Chinese countryside. However, I found the illustration to be somewhat plain. While it was an accurate portrayal of the real Chinese countryside, it didn’t capture the magical essence I wanted to convey. (Upon Isamel's request, I illustrated a flying pickle as a placeholder obstacle)<br><br>I also realized that representing the platform in two dimensions would make the design clearer and more visually effective.</p>", "single": false}, {"br": "5px", "t": "box", "w": 445, "h": 251, "kids": [{"br": "5px", "t": "img", "w": 445, "h": 251, "src": "/images/cs/zOlu1BWM3wXmdMXifeOKZ5TmYE.webp", "fit": "cover", "pos": "50% 50%", "abs": [0, 0]}], "frame": 1}], "fill": 1, "stack": 1}, {"t": "box", "w": 900, "h": 300, "flex": "row|20px|0px|center|center|nowrap", "kids": [{"t": "box", "w": 440, "h": 284, "flex": "column|10px|0px|center|center|nowrap", "kids": [{"t": "text", "w": 440, "h": 63, "html": "<p style=\"font-family:var(--sans);font-size:15px;line-height:22.5px;color:rgb(77, 77, 77);letter-spacing:-0.3px\">One of my concept sketches depicted the cat on the rooftops of Chinese shops. While it was a cute idea, I felt the perspective was too close to the cat, limiting the view of the broader environment.</p>", "fill": 1, "single": false}, {"br": "5px", "t": "box", "w": 440, "h": 211, "kids": [{"br": "5px", "t": "img", "w": 440, "h": 211, "src": "/images/cs/Hz5abCpOrxUGpkUD0a9A53MXY.webp", "fit": "cover", "pos": "50% 50%", "abs": [0, 0]}], "frame": 1}]}, {"t": "box", "w": 440, "h": 300, "flex": "column|10px|0px|center|center|nowrap", "kids": [{"t": "text", "w": 440, "h": 63, "html": "<p style=\"font-family:var(--sans);font-size:15px;line-height:22.5px;color:rgb(77, 77, 77);letter-spacing:-0.3px\">The environment I ultimately settled on featured a bridge as the platform, with a small town in the background and a lake inspired by Xihu, a famous lake in Hangzhou.</p>", "fill": 1, "single": false}, {"br": "5px", "t": "box", "w": 440, "h": 227, "kids": [{"br": "5px", "t": "img", "w": 440, "h": 227, "src": "/images/cs/ak5YZ1Q9smctUgsC1vGOw8Pv8I.webp", "fit": "cover", "pos": "50% 50%", "abs": [0, 0]}], "frame": 1}]}], "fill": 1, "stack": 1}], "fill": 1}], "fill": 1}, {"reveal": 1, "t": "box", "w": 900, "h": 458, "flex": "column|8px|0px|center|center|nowrap", "clip": 1, "kids": [{"id": "03-style", "t": "text", "w": 900, "h": 21, "html": "<h5 style=\"font-family:var(--mono);font-size:14px;line-height:21px;color:rgb(210, 105, 53)\">STYLE &amp; ITERNATION</h5>", "fill": 1, "single": true}, {"t": "box", "w": 900, "h": 421, "flex": "column|8px|0px|flex-start|center|nowrap", "clip": 1, "kids": [{"t": "text", "w": 600, "h": 38, "html": "<h3 style=\"font-family:var(--serif);font-size:24px;line-height:30px;color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">A touch of whimsy to build this world…</h3>", "single": true}, {"t": "text", "w": 600, "h": 84, "html": "<p style=\"font-family:var(--sans);font-size:15px;line-height:22.5px;color:rgb(77, 77, 77);letter-spacing:-0.3px\">After presenting my first fully rendered background draft to my co-creator Isamel, she suggested making it “MORE WHIMSICAL” for a livelier touch. I completely agreed. While the overall mood came across as intended, adding playful elements would create a stronger personal connection. So, I (subtly) incorporated the following:</p>", "single": false}, {"br": "5px", "t": "box", "w": 900, "h": 283, "kids": [{"br": "5px", "t": "img", "w": 900, "h": 283, "src": "/images/cs/q08myAImNeJrx2ZieLV9e00cAYk.webp", "fit": "cover", "pos": "50% 50%", "abs": [0, 0]}], "frame": 1}], "fill": 1}], "fill": 1}, {"reveal": 1, "t": "box", "w": 900, "h": 2114, "flex": "column|32px|0px|center|center|nowrap", "clip": 1, "kids": [{"t": "box", "w": 900, "h": 1271, "flex": "column|8px|0px|flex-start|center|nowrap", "clip": 1, "kids": [{"id": "04-animation", "t": "text", "w": 900, "h": 21, "html": "<h5 style=\"font-family:var(--mono);font-size:14px;line-height:21px;color:rgb(210, 105, 53)\">ANIMATION</h5>", "fill": 1, "single": true}, {"t": "text", "w": 600, "h": 38, "html": "<h3 style=\"font-family:var(--serif);font-size:24px;line-height:30px;color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Animating the lost cat</h3>", "single": true}, {"t": "text", "w": 600, "h": 126, "html": "<p style=\"font-family:var(--sans);font-size:15px;line-height:22.5px;color:rgb(77, 77, 77);letter-spacing:-0.3px\">One my my biggest challenges was learning how to animate. I’ve never animated previously, so I was pretty nervious for this part. Everything was animated on Procreate, as Furward was created before Procreate Dreams was released. After watching a couple of tutorials on Youtube, I started with a few sketches in my sketchbook that indicate the “key” parts of a cat’s walking cycle. To help me understand the form of a cat and it’s walking process, I took videos of my cat walking, and watched videos online.</p>", "single": false}, {"t": "box", "w": 900, "h": 199, "kids": [{"t": "img", "w": 900, "h": 199, "src": "/images/cs/KzmhLMcCc8AQdL4OpZc4PwhIsg.webp", "fit": "cover", "pos": "50% 50%", "fill": 1}]}, {"t": "box", "w": 900, "h": 413, "flex": "row|20px|0px|center|center|nowrap", "kids": [{"t": "box", "w": 440, "h": 379, "flex": "column|10px|0px|center|center|nowrap", "kids": [{"t": "text", "w": 440, "h": 63, "html": "<p style=\"font-family:var(--sans);font-size:15px;line-height:22.5px;color:rgb(77, 77, 77);letter-spacing:-0.3px\">My first iteration of a cat’s walk was pretty wonky. I only realized that the left back leg’s walking cycle was too big for the rest of the cat after I completed the animation.</p>", "fill": 1, "single": false}, {"t": "box", "w": 440, "h": 306, "kids": [{"t": "img", "w": 440, "h": 306, "src": "/images/cs/75G5ygRHjrpvskLtYnKlYVSLK2Y.webp", "fit": "cover", "pos": "50% 50%", "fill": 1}]}]}, {"t": "box", "w": 440, "h": 413, "flex": "column|10px|0px|center|center|nowrap", "kids": [{"t": "text", "w": 440, "h": 42, "html": "<p style=\"font-family:var(--sans);font-size:15px;line-height:22.5px;color:rgb(77, 77, 77);letter-spacing:-0.3px\">After refining, and then eventually deciding to change the character’s fur patterns, the cat began to walk more normally.</p>", "fill": 1, "single": false}, {"t": "box", "w": 440, "h": 361, "kids": [{"t": "img", "w": 440, "h": 361, "src": "/images/cs/T3SnBu0R8Tswhdx89gf9IGw9M.webp", "fit": "cover", "pos": "50% 50%", "fill": 1}]}]}], "fill": 1, "stack": 1}, {"t": "box", "w": 900, "h": 434, "flex": "row|20px|0px|center|center|nowrap", "kids": [{"t": "box", "w": 440, "h": 434, "flex": "column|10px|0px|center|center|nowrap", "kids": [{"t": "text", "w": 440, "h": 63, "html": "<p style=\"font-family:var(--sans);font-size:15px;line-height:22.5px;color:rgb(77, 77, 77);letter-spacing:-0.3px\">After illustrating the cat’s walk, I was ready to become more ambitious with the crawl . I abstracted the crawl so overenhance the “pudginess” of the cat, which I felt added a playful touch.</p>", "fill": 1, "single": false}, {"t": "box", "w": 440, "h": 361, "kids": [{"t": "img", "w": 440, "h": 361, "src": "/images/cs/cv4pMF7xSzIwc3PfD789swQPY84.webp", "fit": "cover", "pos": "50% 50%", "fill": 1}]}]}, {"t": "box", "w": 440, "h": 434, "flex": "column|10px|0px|center|center|nowrap", "kids": [{"t": "text", "w": 440, "h": 63, "html": "<p style=\"font-family:var(--sans);font-size:15px;line-height:22.5px;color:rgb(77, 77, 77);letter-spacing:-0.3px\">Unlike the original <em style=\"font-family:var(--sans);font-size:15px;line-height:22.5px;color:rgb(77, 77, 77);font-style:italic;letter-spacing:-0.3px\">no internet dinosaur</em>, the cat is a long sprite. Thus, we had to further space apart the obstacles to ensure the cat had enough space to land.</p>", "fill": 1, "single": false}, {"t": "box", "w": 440, "h": 361, "kids": [{"t": "img", "w": 440, "h": 361, "src": "/images/cs/Tpr2razzo53s46ymfGh4USriBSE.webp", "fit": "cover", "pos": "50% 50%", "fill": 1}]}]}], "fill": 1, "stack": 1}], "fill": 1}, {"t": "box", "w": 900, "h": 436, "flex": "column|8px|0px|flex-start|center|nowrap", "clip": 1, "kids": [{"t": "text", "w": 600, "h": 38, "html": "<h3 style=\"font-family:var(--serif);font-size:24px;line-height:30px;color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Putting it all together</h3>", "single": true}, {"t": "text", "w": 600, "h": 210, "html": "<p style=\"font-family:var(--sans);font-size:15px;line-height:22.5px;color:rgb(77, 77, 77);letter-spacing:-0.3px\">Since Furward's game concept is simple, the art style becomes the most prominent medium of storytelling.<br><br>Creating the final map included hours of compiling inspiration images, desperately trying to remember how I felt when I went to China, and experimentation with rendering. Along the way, my art style changed, and so did the colours. In total, the background took around a month to fully complete!<br><br>From start to finish, the entire process of illustrating, experimenting, and rendering the map took around a month. The map is a single long illustration that can be repeated.</p>", "single": false}, {"br": "5px", "t": "box", "w": 900, "h": 101, "kids": [{"br": "5px", "t": "img", "w": 900, "h": 101, "src": "/images/cs/EylWOzJIYteKF4JJ0OJAv68dLs.webp", "fit": "cover", "pos": "50% 50%", "abs": [0, 0]}], "frame": 1}, {"t": "text", "w": 600, "h": 63, "html": "<p style=\"font-family:var(--sans);font-size:15px;line-height:22.5px;color:rgb(77, 77, 77);letter-spacing:-0.3px\">In total, Furward has 3 main layers. The further back the layer the more slowly it cycles through in relation to the other layers. The sky layer cycles the slowest, while the platform is the quickest.</p>", "single": false}], "fill": 1}, {"br": "5px", "t": "box", "w": 900, "h": 342, "kids": [{"br": "5px", "t": "img", "w": 900, "h": 342, "src": "/images/cs/Qx4R0r7CZr2qv8pYFfavVEQ5BHk.webp", "fit": "cover", "pos": "50% 50%", "abs": [0, 0]}], "frame": 1}], "fill": 1}, {"reveal": 1, "bg": "rgba(252, 248, 237, 0)", "t": "box", "w": 900, "h": 794, "flex": "column|32px|0px|center|center|nowrap", "clip": 1, "kids": [{"t": "box", "w": 900, "h": 383, "flex": "column|8px|0px|flex-start|center|nowrap", "clip": 1, "kids": [{"id": "05-expansion", "t": "text", "w": 900, "h": 21, "html": "<h5 style=\"font-family:var(--mono);font-size:14px;line-height:21px;color:rgb(210, 105, 53)\">EXPANSION</h5>", "fill": 1, "single": true}, {"t": "text", "w": 600, "h": 38, "html": "<h3 style=\"font-family:var(--serif);font-size:24px;line-height:30px;color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Night mode</h3>", "single": true}, {"t": "text", "w": 600, "h": 210, "html": "<p style=\"font-family:var(--sans);font-size:15px;line-height:22.5px;color:rgb(77, 77, 77);letter-spacing:-0.3px\">After completing the \"day\" version of the map, I realized I wanted to continue developing the game. I also felt it would be a great opportunity to showcase more aspects of China.<br>‍<br>Luckily, I still had ideas for Furward in my sketchbook! I chose to illustrate the city, drawing heavy inspiration from Shanghai, my dad's hometown. To create a sense of unity between the worlds, I designed the night mode to complement the day mode, using complementary colors for both.<br>‍<br>Illustrating the night mode was much faster since I had already established the style and color scheme. Additionally, I had gained more experience in being decisive and sketching thumbnails.</p>", "single": false}, {"br": "5px", "t": "box", "w": 900, "h": 90, "kids": [{"br": "5px", "t": "img", "w": 900, "h": 90, "src": "/images/cs/h6sUewRIrMNvvxDZ6Gb3y1i7hQY.webp", "fit": "cover", "pos": "50% 50%", "abs": [0, 0]}], "frame": 1}], "fill": 1}, {"t": "box", "w": 900, "h": 379, "flex": "column|8px|0px|flex-start|center|nowrap", "clip": 1, "kids": [{"t": "text", "w": 600, "h": 38, "html": "<h3 style=\"font-family:var(--serif);font-size:24px;line-height:30px;color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Easter eggs to create cohesion</h3>", "single": true}, {"t": "text", "w": 600, "h": 42, "html": "<p style=\"font-family:var(--sans);font-size:15px;line-height:22.5px;color:rgb(77, 77, 77);letter-spacing:-0.3px\">I allowed myself to take a few more creative liberties with the night mode. To make the game feel more cohesive, I included subtle details in the night mode that allude back to day mode!</p>", "single": false}, {"br": "5px", "t": "box", "w": 900, "h": 283, "kids": [{"br": "5px", "t": "img", "w": 900, "h": 283, "src": "/images/cs/KsYpXUcqCsYQXSnnSsJ3bmjP9Y.webp", "fit": "cover", "pos": "50% 50%", "abs": [0, 0]}], "frame": 1}], "fill": 1}], "fill": 1}, {"reveal": 1, "t": "box", "w": 900, "h": 706, "flex": "column|32px|0px|center|center|nowrap", "clip": 1, "kids": [{"t": "box", "w": 900, "h": 706, "flex": "column|16px|0px|flex-start|center|nowrap", "clip": 1, "kids": [{"t": "box", "w": 900, "h": 351, "flex": "column|8px|0px|flex-start|center|nowrap", "clip": 1, "kids": [{"id": "06-reflection", "t": "text", "w": 900, "h": 21, "html": "<h5 style=\"font-family:var(--mono);font-size:14px;line-height:21px;color:rgb(210, 105, 53)\">REFLECTION &amp; NEXT STEPS</h5>", "fill": 1, "single": true}, {"t": "text", "w": 600, "h": 38, "html": "<h3 style=\"font-family:var(--serif);font-size:24px;line-height:30px;color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Some next steps</h3>", "single": true}, {"t": "text", "w": 600, "h": 276, "html": "<p style=\"font-family:var(--sans);font-size:15px;line-height:22.5px;color:rgb(77, 77, 77);letter-spacing:-0.3px\">Since this was our first time creating a game, we agreed to keep it pretty simple as a 2D platformer as our MVP. However, we have many plans of expanding Furward and fine tuning the game!</p><p style=\"margin-top:15px;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:15px;line-height:22.5px;color:rgb(77, 77, 77);letter-spacing:-0.3px\">After releasing Furward and play testing multiple times, I felt that the obstacles blend into the background a little bit <em style=\"font-family:var(--sans);font-size:15px;line-height:22.5px;color:rgb(77, 77, 77);font-style:italic;letter-spacing:-0.3px\">too well</em>. Making them glow may be a good idea for making them more obvious to the player, but some players reported that htey liked the extra challenge.</p><p style=\"margin-top:15px;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:15px;line-height:22.5px;color:rgb(77, 77, 77);letter-spacing:-0.3px\">I also felt that much of the foreground and background appear flat at times. Incorporating small animations such as swaying leaves, ripling water, twinkling stars and moving characters may bring Furward more to life.</p><p style=\"margin-top:15px;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:15px;line-height:22.5px;color:rgb(77, 77, 77);letter-spacing:-0.3px\">The immediate next step me and Isamel would like to include is a scoring system and a way for players to share their scores with their audience.</p>", "single": false}], "fill": 1}, {"t": "box", "w": 900, "h": 193, "flex": "column|8px|0px|flex-start|center|nowrap", "clip": 1, "kids": [{"t": "text", "w": 600, "h": 38, "html": "<h3 style=\"font-family:var(--serif);font-size:24px;line-height:30px;color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Done is better than perfect</h3>", "single": true}, {"t": "text", "w": 600, "h": 147, "html": "<p style=\"font-family:var(--sans);font-size:15px;line-height:22.5px;color:rgb(77, 77, 77);letter-spacing:-0.3px\">The first few weeks of creating Furward passed really slowly. As my first large scale project, it was very easy to get lost in the rendering and making sure everything was pixel-perfect (I ended up vectorizing it later). Many hours were spent on miniscule details that had an insignificant impact on the game, and it made the entire process very tedious. Obsessing over small details was the main reason why the drawing process to complete the day map took two months. The \"night\" mode was significiantly faster, as I realized that I should be focusing on the bigger picture.</p>", "single": false}], "fill": 1}, {"t": "box", "w": 900, "h": 130, "flex": "column|8px|0px|flex-start|center|nowrap", "clip": 1, "kids": [{"t": "text", "w": 600, "h": 38, "html": "<h3 style=\"font-family:var(--serif);font-size:24px;line-height:30px;color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Make firm decisions</h3>", "single": true}, {"t": "text", "w": 600, "h": 84, "html": "<p style=\"font-family:var(--sans);font-size:15px;line-height:22.5px;color:rgb(77, 77, 77);letter-spacing:-0.3px\">As a person who suffers from choice paralysis when it comes to the smallest things like hand soap scents, I knew that I could not afford to be indecisive when making this game, because it would drag out the process for too long. Rather than obsessing over finding the right colors for my maps, it was easier to just begin colouring and then worry later.</p>", "single": false}], "fill": 1}], "fill": 1}], "fill": 1}]}, "accent": "rgb(210, 105, 53)"}